            <div xml:id="d972">

                <pb facs="0853" n="841" xml:id="pg841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.796/192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-13T14:00:00-05:00">July 13, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. After a long conference with President-elect who arrived Quito yesterday, he
                    states that he favors introduction of services by Panagra as outlined by the
                    Department: That he is not in favor of arbitrary cancellation of any contract
                    but thinks that study might reveal violations by Sedta. Investigation is being
                    made now. Please refer to my telegram No. 144, July 9, 6 p.m. and 146, July 10,
                    10 a.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d972-f1"/></p>
                <p>In any event the question of financing the elimination remains.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
